  "_read_first": "Use docs/updating.md to request a published update. The request starts verified release selection. The deployed layout comes from the recorded tool. Read update/pristine.json from the pinned release. The published updater preserves optional client edits and stops on required collisions. Older same-folder updaters use the legacy refresh lists: never stop to ask and never replace a file the client has changed under those lists.",
  "_what": "Legacy refresh/remove lists remain for older harnesses, except their three retired .claude skill sources. deployment is the source-to-destination and ownership contract for separate client repositories; select exactly one recorded tool. Contract: docs/updating.md and deployment._contract.",
  "_regenerate": "Maintain deployment entries for every skills/*/SKILL.md. Historical Spec Kit paths are retired only when they still match shipped fingerprints. Run node tests/helpers/pristine.mjs --write after release edits.",
