  "never_touch": {
    "status/status.json": "the client's own record for pairing, stages, packages, and choices. On success the published updater records template_version, applied_release, an appended note, and any explicitly retired checklist keys.",
    "status/send-log.md": "the client's own record of every send decision and verdict, content-free (since 1.5.0)",
    "status/no-contact.md": "the client's own no-contact list, for good (since 1.5.0)",
    "status/waiting.md": "the client's list of messages waiting for them, rewritten by every run (since 1.5.0)",
    "status/shift-log.md": "the client's work history",
    "status/work-log.md": "the client's work history: one line per finished task they asked for (since 1.1.0)",
    "status/shifts/": "the wake-up files written for this machine by status/schedule.mjs: full paths and schedules that only make sense here (since 1.2.0)",
    "memory/ (everything but README.md)": "the client's own memory \u2014 facts, logs, lessons, the index; an update improves the notebook's binding, never its pages",
    "agent/knowledge-base/01..07*.md": "the client's business, captured in their words",
    ".claude/agents/ (everything but nothing \u2014 the whole directory)": "the client's hired team; the roster README carries their rows",
    ".claude/skills/ (any skill not in the refresh list)": "skills the client taught",
    ".update-backup/": "prior updates' safety copies",
    "anything not in the refresh or remove lists": "refresh may write its paths, remove may delete its paths \u2014 nothing else may be touched at all. The two lists are the whole permission"
  },
  "_remove": "Paths pruned on update, with the same backup-first safety as refresh (docs/updating.md steps 3 and 4b). A path lands here when a release retires it; it never returns to refresh. A directory the prune empties is deleted too.",
